d{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(-1\\right)}\\\\\n&=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139547574 17592186576411 true] [17592186761001 1080 "-\\frac{1}{14}" 13194139547574 17592186576411 true] [17592186761001 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547574 17592186576411 true] [17592186761001 1083 #uuid "17c1a001-59d1-5ddb-b46a-5df5b4db950e" 13194139547574 17592186576411 true] [17592186761002 1068 #edb/ref 17592186761012 13194139547574 17592186576411 true] [17592186761002 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139547574 17592186576411 true] [17592186761002 1071 "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=(x-2)(x^{2}-x)\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(2,0\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139547574 17592186576411 true] [17592186761002 1072 #uuid "22201f9d-6ca9-5d62-bd59-8395f61f8ad5" 13194139547574 17592186576411 true] [17592186761002 1074 "Let $f(x)=(x-2)(x^{2}-x)$. Expand and combine like terms before differentiating.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=x^{3}-x^{2}-2x^{2}+2x\\\\\n&=x^{3}-3x^{2}+2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=3x^{2}-6x+2\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(2,0\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(2)&=3\\left(2\\right)^{2}-6\\left(2\\right)+2\\\\\n&=12-12+2\\\\\n&=2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(2\\right)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139547574 17592186576411 true] [17592186761003 1068 #edb/ref 17592186761013 13194139547574 17592186576411 true] [17592186761003 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139547574 17592186576411 true] [17592186761003 1071 "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=(x-2)(x^{2}+x)\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(2,0\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}" 131941395475